WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.437
American Express. Enterprise Technology Services. Tools training.

2
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.883
Strategy is planned in Targetprocess.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.227
Delivery happens in Jira Cloud.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.957
The integration between them decides whether strategy actually reaches the backlog.

5
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.364
Linking Strategic Epics.

6
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.901
A Strategic Epic is your top portfolio tier: a Portfolio Epic, or a custom level above it.

7
00:00:32.951 --> 00:00:34.602
Start with the hierarchy.

8
00:00:34.652 --> 00:00:38.351
A Feature in Targetprocess pairs with an Epic in Jira.

9
00:00:38.401 --> 00:00:42.846
User Stories become Jira Stories, linked to their Epic through Epic Link.

10
00:00:42.896 --> 00:00:46.957
Bugs and tasks follow through Parent of, or the link type you choose.

11
00:00:47.007 --> 00:00:52.285
In the tool, a Portfolio Epic lists its Features, and each one shows its Jira key.

12
00:00:53.007 --> 00:00:57.879
In Jira, that Feature is an Epic, with its stories and bugs as child issues.

13
00:00:58.607 --> 00:01:05.357
Two rules. User Stories always go through a Feature. And sub-tasks never roll up to portfolio level.

14
00:01:05.407 --> 00:01:07.911
There are two ways to link a Strategic Epic.

15
00:01:08.207 --> 00:01:17.772
Pattern A: the epic becomes a Jira project. Its Jira Project Key field, plus JS routing, sends every child item into that project.

16
00:01:17.822 --> 00:01:24.486
Pattern B: Features are pushed as Jira Epics, into a shared portfolio project, or each team's own.

17
00:01:24.536 --> 00:01:27.893
Either way, everything below the epic syncs the same way.

18
00:01:29.136 --> 00:01:33.816
Setup. First, a product specialist enables the integration for your org.

19
00:01:33.866 --> 00:01:38.759
Then in Settings, Integrations, click Add integration, and choose Jira Cloud.

20
00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:41.655
Pick Server only for Jira Data Center.

21
00:01:42.466 --> 00:01:49.450
Next, map the types. Feature to Epic. User Story to Story. Bug to Bug. Team Iteration to Sprint.

22
00:01:52.266 --> 00:01:56.946
Under Project routing, pair your Targetprocess projects with Jira projects.

23
00:01:56.996 --> 00:02:01.761
Or turn on JS routing to route by the epic's Jira Project Key.

24
00:02:02.596 --> 00:02:07.639
Then set the filters. They decide what auto-pushes, and what an import can bring in.

25
00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:12.367
And with auto-push on, changes flow without anyone clicking.

26
00:02:15.996 --> 00:02:19.311
Now link the work. Open the Feature's Synced Work tab.

27
00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:25.692
Click Push as new to create it in Jira, or Link to Existing for an issue that's already there.

28
00:02:25.742 --> 00:02:28.459
It's synced, and the Jira key appears right here.

29
00:02:29.342 --> 00:02:32.870
On any card, the External ID clicks straight through to Jira.

30
00:02:33.342 --> 00:02:36.891
And in Jira, the issue shows it came from Targetprocess.

31
00:02:39.342 --> 00:02:43.254
Or bring work in from Jira. Enter a J.Q.L. query.

32
00:02:43.342 --> 00:02:47.830
Click Forecast to see the issue count and estimated time before you run it.

33
00:02:48.742 --> 00:02:57.411
Then import. Bring in only the Epics. Their stories and bugs come along, and re-importing updates items. It never duplicates them.

34
00:02:57.742 --> 00:03:01.334
From then on, changes sync as they happen, within your filters.

35
00:03:01.542 --> 00:03:03.811
The menu adds three manual actions.

36
00:03:04.342 --> 00:03:08.169
Push Updates resends every mapped field. You'll rarely need it.

37
00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:12.365
Pull Updates refreshes from Jira, except child collections' fields.

38
00:03:12.415 --> 00:03:14.066
And Unlink stops syncing.

39
00:03:15.015 --> 00:03:19.653
Team Iterations sync with Jira Sprints: name, description and dates.

40
00:03:21.015 --> 00:03:22.197
Watch-outs.

41
00:03:22.247 --> 00:03:26.969
Unlinking with auto-push on can create duplicates. Fix your filters first.

42
00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:34.003
Batch push skips Extendable Domain types, so a custom Strategic Epic level may need linking item by item.

43
00:03:34.053 --> 00:03:36.152
Tasks only import with their parent.

44
00:03:36.253 --> 00:03:40.037
And when something fails, check Settings, Diagnostic and Logs.

45
00:03:45.453 --> 00:03:50.731
Map the hierarchy. Route by project key. Import the epics. Watch the logs.

46
00:03:52.853 --> 00:03:56.381
American Express. Enterprise Technology Services.

